# LehroCode IDE/Harness UI — Implementation Plan

## Problem Statement

The reference image shows a **full IDE/harness interface** — a code-editor-centric layout with agent streams, system graphs, terminal panels, and AI suggestions. The existing project only has the **Project Portal** (admin dashboard with sidebar navigation, CRUD pages for projects/news/users/etc.), which is a separate management view.

The IDE/Harness UI is the **core product experience** — where developers interact with LehroCode's multi-agent orchestration in real-time. It does **not** exist yet.

![Reference Image](file:///d:/lehrocode/LehroCode.png)

---

## Proposed Architecture

The IDE will live at a dedicated `/ide` route, completely separate from the `(admin)` layout. It gets its own full-bleed layout with no sidebar/header from the portal — instead, it has its own purpose-built chrome.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The IDE is a **completely separate layout** from the admin portal. It has its own top bar, its own panel system, and fills the entire viewport. No admin sidebar, no admin header.

