## Design Decisions

### Why static code rendering instead of Monaco?
The reference shows a read-only code display with AI suggestions — not a full text editor. Using styled `<pre>` blocks keeps the bundle lean (~0 KB added vs ~2MB for Monaco) and gives us pixel-perfect control over the syntax highlighting colors matching the reference's dark theme. The AI suggestion diff panel is custom UI regardless.

### Why a separate `/ide` route instead of modifying the dashboard?
The dashboard already works well as a project management portal. The IDE is a fundamentally different experience — full-bleed, no portal sidebar, custom chrome. Mixing them would compromise both.

### CSS Grid for the IDE layout
The five-zone layout (top bar, left panel, center+bottom, right panel) maps naturally to CSS Grid with `grid-template-areas`. This gives precise control over panel sizing and future resizability.

